[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5644490068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5644490068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5644490068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUHAVVA","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T07:33:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T07:35:07Z","body":"Interesting. The error list in the script editor always felt crammed. And the jumping bottom bar when there is a long error obscuring the last line of the code is very irritating. I would suggest, if possible, to add an ability to expand the text of the diagnostics so that by default it is truncated but you can click on it to expand it. Also maybe the line/col text can be placed before the error text or in its own column like \"7:15\" (or just a line number) so you can quickly skim through and get an idea where the error/warning is? (Like it was before)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5644490068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5645472126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5645472126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5645472126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUH8Rfg","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T11:00:36Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T11:07:41Z","body":"I think a format like this would be much better for the bottom diagnostic copy that I previously proposed because people can get a short concise error/warning diagnose form the hover copy and for details the bottom one being more detail makes more sense like other IDEs:\r\n\r\n`path/to/file.gd:10:9: warning: [UNUSED PARAMETER] The parameter \"delta\" is never used in the function \"process()\".`\r\n// something like this or in some other format for the info.\r\n\r\nIncluding the file path alongside the line and column numbers adds a lot of value. For better or worse, many people copy these diagnostics into AI tools for help, and having the full context (including the path) makes a big difference IMO.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"621\" height=\"326\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7330e18-4bb3-4618-b818-c5b417845703\" />\r\n ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5645472126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5646960786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5646960786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5646960786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUJXIkg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T15:52:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T15:52:10Z","body":"Thanks for the feedback!\r\n\r\n> I would suggest, if possible, to add an ability to expand the text of the diagnostics so that by default it is truncated but you can click on it to expand it.\r\n\r\n@romgerman I would love this as well, or even just allowing the text in a row to wrap and expand the height of the row in the process. From a quick Google search about wrapping text in TreeItems, [at least one person claims it's infeasible because it would cause performance issues for very large/long trees (thousands of items)](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/how-do-i-wrap-text-in-a-treeitem/4105/2). With the number of diagnostics that are likely to show up in this specific tree, I don't think it would be an issue though. I might file a proposal for adding text wrapping/multiline support to tree items, and perhaps even explore an implementation myself when I have time.\r\n\r\n> Also maybe the line/col text can be placed before the error text or in its own column like \"7:15\" (or just a line number) so you can quickly skim through and get an idea where the error/warning is? (Like it was before)\r\n\r\nMoving it to before the diagnostic text would be quite easy; moving it to its own column could certainly be done as well, although I need to figure out how to make columns size themselves to only fit the width of their content.\r\n\r\n> I think a format like this would be much better for the bottom diagnostic copy that I previously proposed because people can get a short concise error/warning diagnose form the hover copy and for details the bottom one being more detail makes more sense like other IDEs:\r\n> ```\r\n> path/to/file.gd:10:9: warning: [UNUSED PARAMETER] The parameter \"delta\" is never used in the function \"process()\".\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n@shiva-kar We could make that change; additionally/alternatively, it could be something the user chooses, either via an editor setting or via multiple copy options, e.g., \"Copy Diagnostic Message\" and \"Copy Full Diagnostic\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5646960786/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5667776888","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5667776888","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5667776888,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUdNpeA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T17:10:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T17:10:43Z","body":"Due to the limitations of the Tree node, I decided to try replacing that approach with just building a stack of custom components that each display a diagnostic. What I have so far on that branch is looking pretty good to me:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2145\" height=\"1886\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-09-14 at 10 03 40 AM@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc576771-15ff-4514-bbb2-c59913f8a334\" />\r\n\r\nDouble-clicking a diagnostic takes you to the line and column where the diagnostic starts, if it has such information.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to test it, the branch is available here: https://github.com/Meorge/godot/tree/feat/diagnostics-list-no-tree\r\nPlease let me know what you think of this look! (I've kept the branch with the Tree implementation as well, so if we decide to revert to that, it doesn't have to be recreated.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5667776888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704531283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5704531283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5704531283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVAQ9Uw","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T21:08:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T21:08:19Z","body":"> If you'd like to test it, the branch is available here\r\n\r\nI've tried but didn't find the new diagnostics design. I also needed to add some includes to make it compile. Sorry I'm maybe missed it but they are not under the script editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704531283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704636811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5704636811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5704636811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVAXZiw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T21:17:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T21:17:02Z","body":"I see that the CI for the new branch is failing on many platforms, so I'll have to go in soon and get that fixed so it will compile. As for finding the design itself, are you sure you were using my branch titled `feat/diagnostics-no-tree` with latest commit `b23f1f6e37352a188d1bde888dd5de5d0efb7383`? If you happened to compile a different branch or commit from my fork, it may not show up. From the commit [here](https://github.com/Meorge/godot/commit/b23f1f6e37352a188d1bde888dd5de5d0efb7383) I can see all the code for it, so it should be there...\r\n\r\nI'm currently wrapping up fixes for a different PR, and once I'm done with those, I'll hop over to this one and try to get it all fixed up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704636811/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5708100118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123434#issuecomment-5708100118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123434","id":5708100118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVDqyFg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"c